 topic=("Bats in Centennial attics",
        "<p>Bats return to the same roost each summer, and mothers raise pups in attics from about June through August. Sealing openings during that time traps young inside. The right approach is exclusion: one-way devices over entry points once pups can fly, usually late summer or early fall, then sealing all gaps. If a bat is found in a room where someone was sleeping, contact your doctor or public health office about rabies. See <a href=\"/services/wildlife-removal/\">bat removal</a> and <a href=\"/services/rodent-control/\">mouse control</a>.</p>"),
